# Clean URLs for the policy pages. Netlify usually strips .html on its own, but
# these are explicit because Razorpay's and Google's reviewers will hit the exact
# URLs you type into their forms, and a 404 there costs you the approval.
/privacy      /privacy.html    200
/terms        /terms.html      200
/refund       /refund.html     200
/cancellation /refund.html     200
/contact      /contact.html    200

# Old in-app anchors, in case they are linked anywhere.
/privacy-policy      /privacy.html   301
/terms-and-conditions /terms.html    301

# Do NOT add an apex-to-www redirect here. Set the primary domain in
# Netlify > Domain management instead; Netlify then issues the 301 itself, and a
# hand-written rule on top of that can produce a redirect loop.
